1. Live GUI witness
src/frontends/gui/bridge.rs:161-188 adds a test-fixtures-only observer. The
actual Bridge::create worker registers its Config redactor, then invokes the
observer synchronously immediately before Host::new. Production builds have
no observer field/API. tests/capability_delivery.rs:588 starts that real live
bridge in an isolated child test process with a private 0600 file. At the
pre-Host boundary it captures whether Set::scrub(value) == <redacted>, asserts
GuiLiveCapabilityRegisteredBeforeHost, then waits for a ready session and
closes it. It uses no window, display interaction or test-thread environment
mutation. Deleting only the live loader fails that assertion, exit 101;
restoring its exact bytes passes, exit 0.

2. Per-face controls
scripts/test-capability-control.py now covers eight paths, with one exact test
per mutation. Headless/seat/ACP share one production loader, so those mutations
skip registration only for the selected face. GUI replay, live GUI, GUI smoke
and optional live smoke each lose their own call. The legacy-reader control
still replaces the common consumer with a raw-environment reader.

legacy-reader -> HeadlessCapabilityRegistered: 101 -> 0
headless -> HeadlessCapabilityRegistered: 101 -> 0
seat -> SeatCapabilityRegistered: 101 -> 0
ACP -> AcpCapabilityRegistered: 101 -> 0
GUI Bridge::replay -> GuiReplayCapabilityRegistered: 101 -> 0
GUI Bridge::create -> GuiLiveCapabilityRegisteredBeforeHost: 101 -> 0
GUI smoke -> GuiSmokeRegistersCapabilityBeforeRendering: 101 -> 0
optional live smoke -> SmokeCapabilityCheckedBeforeKeySkip: 101 -> 0

Headless/seat/ACP assertions inspect stdout/stderr AND actual session log/blob
bytes. The seat mutation exposes its failure in stored data even when its
compact terminal projection does not print the entire tool output. GUI replay
checks the projected transcript; GUI smoke compares actual offscreen PNG bytes
against explicit redaction. The smoke witness checks the invalid-file refusal
before the isolated no-provider-key skip. The child-test wrapper has a distinct
assertion name, so its generic failure cannot masquerade as the inner proof.
Every mutation requires one running test, exit 101, failed-test output and the
named assertion, then exact source restoration and a successful exact test.
The canonical scripts/test.py command remains unchanged and invokes all cases.
tests/gui_gate.py enables test-fixtures so the live witness also runs in its
ordinary GUI suite.

