3. File-path-specific case (c)
tests/capability_delivery.rs:407 adds a real echo_env server test for profile,
ACP and launcher origins. The fixture reports a capability_file_present boolean
and names, never values. The configured reserved file key is also attempted.
Profile and ACP observations explicitly require BBOXY_CAPABILITY_FILE absent
and an empty BBOXY_* namespace. Launcher --mcp-config explicitly requires that
file variable present. Every origin also executes a real bash tool: printenv,
cat "$BBOXY_CAPABILITY_FILE" and printenv BBOXY_CAPABILITY_FILE yield no reserved
environment/path/value; literal-path output is redacted, including stored data.
The legacy variable is absent from all three MCP process environments.
tests/bin/mcp_fixture.rs adds only that observation boolean.

4. Quiet when unset
src/capability.rs:99 and src/redact.rs:63 distinguish absent configuration from
failed validation. Unset marks initialization complete with no value/refusal;
there is no IO or Notice. A supplied invalid path still runs the existing
descriptor-validated consumer and produces its safe typed refusal.
tests/capability_delivery.rs:321 asserts silent headless startup when unset and
a completed turn, plus typed path/value-free Notices and continuation for set
missing/symlink/mode/content/type failures. The GUI Bridge::replay child test at
:537 covers valid, unset and supplied invalid input; only the invalid case has
a Notice. Its valid case separately checks redaction before projection.
Refusal checks, lowercase canonical format, file ownership/lifetime, redaction
and the launcher MCP exception remain as in the accepted Side B implementation.

